WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.778
The report was already with both donors. Then the
count changed. BasketBrief followed through.

00:00:06.917 --> 00:00:12.343
Small aid groups collect receipts and delivery
counts from different volunteers. A late correction

00:00:12.343 --> 00:00:16.829
leaves the coordinator chasing answers and keeping
both donor reports consistent.

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:24.662
BasketBrief is for Amal, a coordinator. Rana has the
receipt. Sami has the counts. The agent carries

00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:27.199
one evidence trail across both donors.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.046
BasketBrief is a Strands agent that owns the follow-
up work.

00:00:33.217 --> 00:00:39.023
It finds sixty dollars without a receipt and asks
the person who can resolve it. One answer serves

00:00:39.023 --> 00:00:39.793
both reports.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:46.575
Rana answers with a photograph. Nova Pro reads it
through AgentCore Runtime before the review

00:00:46.575 --> 00:00:46.998
starts.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:54.128
The transcription states sixty dollars. The original
stays visible for review. Receipt support is

00:00:54.128 --> 00:00:55.422
not proof of payment.

00:00:56.583 --> 00:01:03.076
Amal approves one exact version, bound to its
content hash. Both donors receive immutable inbox

00:01:03.076 --> 00:01:03.759
snapshots.

00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:08.277
Then the count changes. Eighty-eight, not ninety-
two.

00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:16.409
A hundred loaded. Eighty-eight delivered. Eight
returned. Four unaccounted for, and the old approval

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.101
is refused.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:24.111
That discrepancy says nothing about households.
BasketBrief asks Sami to check storage instead of

00:01:24.111 --> 00:01:25.138
inventing impact.

00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:32.163
Sami confirms twelve returned. The figures
reconcile, and both changes are shown before
approval.

00:01:33.317 --> 00:01:37.541
Northstar keeps the original report and receives the
amendment beside it.

00:01:38.717 --> 00:01:43.085
The Arabic donor receives the same approved evidence
and exact changes.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:50.109
Beyond the guided story, teammates sign in
separately. New evidence and questions reach the
people

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:50.826
responsible.

00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:58.143
A requested receipt completes the original expense,
without counting it twice. Reviewers inspect the

00:01:58.143 --> 00:02:01.223
source. Donors receive only the approved snapshot.

00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:06.367
The model decides what a source means. The code
decides what is allowed.

00:02:08.783 --> 00:02:15.451
Strands and Nova choose tools. AgentCore Runtime
reads images, Memory carries vendor history, and

00:02:15.451 --> 00:02:20.399
deterministic code owns facts, roles, follow-ups,
and approval validity.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:27.025
One hundred twenty-one tests pass, including thirty
adversarial boundary cases. Separate team

00:02:27.025 --> 00:02:31.558
accounts completed the handoff, and a private Gmail
import passed its checks.

00:02:32.717 --> 00:02:38.397
Fictional participants. A live system. BasketBrief
keeps the follow-up moving and every correction

00:02:38.397 --> 00:02:41.933
visible, so the people doing the work can stay with
the work.
